+
+## API Changes
+
+### Internal API (FastAPI endpoints exposed by this service)
+
+No new external-facing REST endpoints. Returns data is written to Postgres for downstream query by reporting tools.
+
+### External API Consumed
+
+| Endpoint | Method | Direction | Auth | Rate Limit |
+|----------|--------|-----------|------|------------|
+| `GET /sellers/v1/sellers/{seller_id}/product_returns` | GET | Outbound (poll) | OAuth2 Bearer | Unknown — to be captured by STORY-007 |
+
+**HTTP Method Semantics (consumed endpoint):**
+
+| Method | Idempotent | Resource Must Exist | Notes |
+|--------|-----------|---------------------|-------|
+| GET | Yes | seller_id must be valid | Returns empty array if no returns exist |
+
+**Rate Limit Design:**
+- [ ] Rate limit values TBD via STORY-007 staging discovery
+- [ ] Polling interval (default 600s) is conservative; adjust after rate limit is known
+- [ ] Retry on 429: exponential backoff starting at 5s, max 3 retries, then skip cycle
+- [ ] Log rate-limit headers (`X-RateLimit-Remaining`, `Retry-After`) on every response
+
+## Database Changes
+
+### Table: `product_returns`
+
+| Column | Type | Constraints | Source Field | Notes |
+|--------|------|-------------|--------------|-------|
+| `id` | `VARCHAR(24)` | PK | `ProductReturn.id` | MongoDB ObjectId format |
+| `order_id` | `VARCHAR(64)` | NULLABLE, INDEX | `ProductReturn.order_id` | Composite `{order_number}-{suffix}`. Soft FK to orders. |
+| `order_number` | `VARCHAR(32)` | NULLABLE | `ProductReturn.order_number` | |
+| `seller_id` | `VARCHAR(32)` | NOT NULL, INDEX | `ProductReturn.seller_id` | |
+| `return_order_number` | `VARCHAR(32)` | NULLABLE | `ProductReturn.return_order_number` | |
+| `tcin` | `VARCHAR(16)` | NULLABLE, INDEX | `ProductReturn.tcin` | Target.com Item Number (like ASIN) |
+| `external_id` | `VARCHAR(64)` | NULLABLE | `ProductReturn.external_id` | Seller SKU |
+| `quantity` | `INTEGER` | NOT NULL, DEFAULT 1 | `ProductReturn.quantity` | |
+| `return_reason` | `VARCHAR(32)` | NULLABLE | `ProductReturn.return_reason` | Raw value from API |
+| `return_reason_known` | `BOOLEAN` | NOT NULL, DEFAULT true | — | `false` when value not in known enum set |
+| `return_date` | `TIMESTAMPTZ` | NULLABLE | `ProductReturn.return_date` | |
+| `created` | `TIMESTAMPTZ` | NULLABLE | `ProductReturn.created` | Target-side creation time |
+| `last_modified` | `TIMESTAMPTZ` | NULLABLE, INDEX | `ProductReturn.last_modified` | Used for cursor-based polling |
+| `created_by` | `VARCHAR(64)` | NULLABLE | `ProductReturn.created_by` | e.g., "SYSTEM" |
+| `last_modified_by` | `VARCHAR(64)` | NULLABLE | `ProductReturn.last_modified_by` | |
+| `is_archived` | `BOOLEAN` | NOT NULL, DEFAULT false | — | Future retention flag; not used in v1 |
+| `ingested_at` | `TIMESTAMPTZ` | NOT NULL, DEFAULT NOW() | — | When GC first saw this record |
+| `updated_at` | `TIMESTAMPTZ` | NOT NULL, DEFAULT NOW() | — | Last upsert time |
+
+**Indexes:**
+- PK: `id`
+- `ix_product_returns_seller_id` on `seller_id`
+- `ix_product_returns_order_id` on `order_id`
+- `ix_product_returns_tcin` on `tcin`
+- `ix_product_returns_last_modified` on `last_modified` (cursor queries)
+- `ix_product_returns_active` partial index on `(seller_id, return_date) WHERE NOT is_archived` (operational queries)
+
+**Upsert strategy:** `INSERT ... ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET` all mutable columns + `updated_at = NOW()`.
+
+### Table: `poll_state`
+
+| Column | Type | Constraints | Notes |
+|--------|------|-------------|-------|
+| `endpoint` | `VARCHAR(128)` | PK | e.g., `product_returns` |
+| `cursor_value` | `VARCHAR(128)` | NULLABLE | High-water mark (ISO 8601 `last_modified` value) |
+| `last_poll_at` | `TIMESTAMPTZ` | NOT NULL | When last poll completed |
+| `records_fetched` | `INTEGER` | NOT NULL, DEFAULT 0 | Count from last poll |
+| `error_count` | `INTEGER` | NOT NULL, DEFAULT 0 | Consecutive errors; reset on success |
+
+**Migration required:** Yes — single Alembic migration creates both tables.
+
+**Migration discipline:** `alembic heads` must return exactly 1 head before PR merge. If multiple heads, create merge migration.
+
+## Implementation Patterns (Adapter/Driver Interactions)
+
+- [ ] **Parameter binding syntax:** httpx query params via `params=dict` (no manual URL interpolation). Seller ID injected into URL path via f-string with validated input only.
+- [ ] **Error handling per adapter:** `httpx.HTTPStatusError` caught → log status + response body → increment `poll_state.error_count` → skip cycle. 429 → exponential backoff. 5xx → log + skip. 4xx (non-429) → log as warning + skip.
+- [ ] **Query generation:** Postgres upsert via SQLAlchemy `insert().on_conflict_do_update()` — parameterized, no string interpolation.
+- [ ] **Pagination strategy:** Target returns endpoint returns a flat array (no pagination documented in OpenAPI spec). If response exceeds 10 MB, log circuit-breaker warning and truncate. Pagination TBD via STORY-007 if discovered.
+
+## Error Handling Strategy
+
+| Error Scenario | Handling | Behavior | Log Fields |
+|----------------|----------|----------|------------|
+| Target API returns 429 | Exponential backoff (5s, 10s, 20s), max 3 retries | Fail-closed: skip cycle, retry next interval | `status=429, retry_after, attempt` |
+| Target API returns 5xx | Log + skip cycle | Fail-closed: increment `error_count` | `status, response_body_preview, endpoint` |
+| Target API returns 4xx (non-429) | Log warning + skip cycle | Fail-closed: likely config error | `status, seller_id, detail` |
+| Target API unreachable (connection error) | Log + skip cycle | Fail-closed: increment `error_count` | `error_type, endpoint, duration_ms` |
+| Unknown `return_reason` value | Store raw value, set `return_reason_known = false` | Fail-open (tag and continue) | `unknown_value, return_id` |
+| `order_id` references non-existent order | Store as-is (nullable soft FK) | Fail-open: reconciliation test catches drift | `order_id, return_id` |
+| Cursor state lost (row deleted) | Fall back to full-fetch + dedup | Fail-safe: dedup absorbs duplicates | `endpoint, fallback_reason` |
+| DB write failure (Postgres down) | Raise, crash poll cycle | Fail-closed: no silent data loss | `error, endpoint` |
+| Response > 10 MB | Circuit breaker: log warning, skip | Fail-closed: prevent OOM | `response_size_bytes, endpoint` |
+
+**Error response format (internal):** RFC 7807 Problem Details for any FastAPI endpoints. Poll loop errors are logged, not returned as HTTP responses.
+
+**What is NOT exposed:** Stack traces, internal file paths, database connection strings, OAuth tokens. Log at DEBUG level only; production runs at INFO.
+
+**Fallback behavior summary:**
+- External API unavailable → fail-closed (skip cycle, no stale data written)
+- Unknown enum → fail-open (tag and continue — data is still valuable)
+- Missing FK target → fail-open (store, reconcile later)
+- Database unavailable → fail-closed (crash cycle, no silent loss)
+
+## Failure Modes Table
+
+| Dependency | Unavailable Behavior | Rationale |
+|------------|---------------------|-----------|
+| Target API | Fail-closed: skip poll cycle, increment `error_count`, retry next interval | No stale/partial data written; dedup makes full-fetch safe on recovery |
+| Postgres | Fail-closed: crash poll cycle, raise exception | Silent data loss is worse than a restart; orchestrator retries |
+| STORY-009 orders table | Fail-open: store return with nullable `order_id`; reconciliation test flags drift | Returns are valuable independently; FK integrity is a quality signal, not a gate |
+
+## Integration Points
+
+| System | Direction | Protocol | Auth | Notes |
+|--------|-----------|----------|------|-------|
+| Target Seller API | Outbound (poll) | HTTPS REST | OAuth2 Bearer | Read-only; `GET` only |
+| Postgres | Bidirectional | SQLAlchemy ORM | Connection string (env var) | Upsert writes + cursor reads |
+| STORY-009 orders table | Read (soft FK check) | Same DB | N/A | Reconciliation query; no hard FK |
+
+## Security Constraints
+
+- [x] **Read-only API access** — no writes to Target API under any circumstance
+- [x] **DI'd client** — `TargetReturnsClient` injected; test suite uses mock
+- [x] **Zero production calls** — `respx` assertion in every test module
+- [x] **No PII in logs** — return records may contain order-level PII; log only IDs and counts, never customer names/addresses
+- [x] **OAuth token handling** — token passed at runtime, never persisted to disk or logged
+- [x] **Seller ID validation** — validate format before URL interpolation (alphanumeric, max 32 chars)
+
+## Performance Considerations
+
+| Metric | Expectation | Design Response |
+|--------|-------------|-----------------|
+| Poll interval | 10 min default (configurable) | `RETURNS_POLL_INTERVAL_SEC` env var |
+| Response size | Unknown (no volume data yet) | 10 MB circuit breaker; monitor in staging |
+| Upsert throughput | Hundreds of records per cycle (estimated) | Bulk `INSERT ... ON CONFLICT` in single transaction |
+| Query patterns | Downstream reporting queries by `seller_id`, `order_id`, `tcin`, `return_date` range | Indexes on all four; partial index for active records |
+| Cursor efficiency | Incremental fetch reduces redundant API calls | `last_modified` high-water mark; fallback to full-fetch if unreliable |
+
+## Operational Readiness
+
+| Concern | Design Decision | Acceptance Criteria |
+|---------|----------------|---------------------|
+| **Health checks** | Poll staleness check: `/health` returns `degraded` if last successful poll > 3× interval | AC-8: `/health` reports poller status |
+| **Metrics** | Log-based metrics in v1: `records_fetched`, `records_upserted`, `poll_duration_ms`, `error_count` per cycle | AC-9: structured JSON logs per poll cycle |
+| **Structured logging** | JSON format, fields: `timestamp`, `level`, `event`, `endpoint`, `seller_id`, `records_fetched`, `records_upserted`, `cursor_value`, `duration_ms`, `error` (if any) | AC-9: all poll cycles emit structured logs |
+| **Alerting needs** | Alert if `error_count >= 5` consecutive failures | Threshold configurable; alert rule defined |
+| **Deployment safety** | Poller is idempotent (dedup); safe to restart at any time | Upsert + cursor = no data loss on restart |
+
+## Async Hazards
+
+| SDK/Library | Sync or Async? | Wrapping Strategy |
+|-------------|----------------|-------------------|
+| `httpx.AsyncClient` | Async (native) | Direct `await` — no wrapping needed |
+| SQLAlchemy 2.0 | Async via `asyncpg` | Use `AsyncSession` + `async_engine`; no sync calls in async context |
+| Alembic | Sync | Alembic runs offline (CLI); not called from async poll loop |
+
+## Startup Dependencies
+
+- [x] `product_returns` table must exist before first poll cycle
+- [x] `poll_state` table must exist before first poll cycle
+- [x] Pattern: `alembic upgrade head` runs in deployment pipeline before app start; poll loop does NOT lazily create tables
+
+## Runtime Configuration
+
+| Setting | Env Var | Default | Notes |
+|---------|---------|---------|-------|
+| Poll interval | `RETURNS_POLL_INTERVAL_SEC` | `600` | Shorter for staging (e.g., 60s) |
+| Seller ID | `TARGET_SELLER_ID` | — (required) | Injected at runtime |
+| Circuit breaker size | `RETURNS_MAX_RESPONSE_BYTES` | `10485760` (10 MB) | Skip cycle if exceeded |
+| Error threshold for alert | `RETURNS_ERROR_THRESHOLD` | `5` | Consecutive failures before alert |
+
+## Constraints
+
+- STORY-007 must complete staging discovery before production deployment (rate limits, auth flow, enum values)
+- STORY-009 orders table must exist for FK reconciliation tests to pass (soft dependency — returns ingest works without it)
+- No bulk update endpoints exist — all Target API operations are per-item/per-call
+- US-based in-house engineering only (Target onboarding constraint)
+
+## Out of Scope
+
+- Physical archive/retention cron (follow-up story after production volume is known)
+- Refund itemization ingest (OQ-21 — pending PM clarification)
+- Cross-channel return analytics (future story combining Target + Amazon returns)
+- Write-back to Target API (read-only scope)
+- Amazon SP-API returns ingest (separate story)
+- UI/dashboard for return data (downstream consumer)
+- Webhook/push integration (Target is poll-only)
+
+## Follow-ups
+
+- Validate `last_modified` ordering assumption during STORY-007 staging discovery
+- Refund itemization data (OQ-21) — escalate to PM if payload reveals line-item fees
+- Physical archive cron when production data volume is known
+- Prometheus `/metrics` endpoint (v2 — log-based metrics sufficient for v1)
+- Shared auth module extraction after STORY-007 completes
+
+## Medium Scope Completeness Checklist
+
+- [x] Component boundaries defined
+- [x] API request/response shapes specified (consumed Target endpoint documented)
+- [x] Database changes documented with migration needs
+- [x] Error handling strategy for each failure scenario
+- [x] Security constraints from seed.md carried forward
+- [x] Integration points identified
+- [x] Out of scope clearly defined
+- [x] Implementation patterns (adapter/driver interactions) specified
+- [x] Operational readiness requirements specified
+- [x] Shared utilities identified and ownership assigned
+- [x] Async hazards documented
